#### these .gitignore entries help prevent sensitive information and 
#### machine-specific configuration from being uploaded to your repository.
 
# Environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
### Ignores files whose names start with .env., such as .env.local and .env.production. Exception: allows .env.example to be tracked, even though it matches the preceding ignore rules.
# Local configuration overrides
application-local.properties
